WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:04.550
As you probably already noticed, the Far From
Home trailer doesn't even slightly acknowledge

00:00:04.550 --> 00:00:09.350
the titanic events of Avengers: Infinity War,
in which half the population of the universe

00:00:09.350 --> 00:00:12.140
succumbed to sudden death, at least temporarily.

00:00:12.140 --> 00:00:17.780
It also seems to sidestep the events of that
movie's forthcoming follow-up, Avengers: Endgame,

00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:22.110
which is set to hit theaters only a couple
of months before the release of Far From Home.

00:00:22.110 --> 00:00:27.320
To the casual moviegoer, it's as though the
fight against Thanos didn't even happen.

00:00:27.320 --> 00:00:31.880
But for dedicated fans of the Marvel Cinematic
Universe, it's pretty weird to see Peter Parker

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:33.570
just suddenly being alive again.

00:00:33.570 --> 00:00:36.260
"Peter, you have to tell me what's going on."

00:00:36.260 --> 00:00:40.530
Instead of walking around looking shell-shocked
and traumatized, the Far From Home trailer

00:00:40.530 --> 00:00:44.960
seems to show the people of the MCU being
back to business as usual.

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:49.760
Happy Hogan is there, Aunt May's there, Nick
Fury's there, and Peter's biggest concern

00:00:49.760 --> 00:00:51.440
seems to be his crush on MJ.

00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:56.140
Instead of going through an existential crisis
after everything he's seen, Peter is back

00:00:56.149 --> 00:01:00.710
to being his plucky self, and has no problem
suiting up to go on an adventure with Nick

00:01:00.710 --> 00:01:01.280
Fury.

00:01:01.700 --> 00:01:04.500
Both of them seem to have recovered from their
deaths incredibly well.

00:01:04.960 --> 00:01:05.640
What's going on?

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:06.660
"Why all the secrecy?

00:01:07.060 --> 00:01:08.060
Why not just tell us?"

00:01:08.060 --> 00:01:10.159
"Any attempt on the director's life had to
look successful."

00:01:10.780 --> 00:01:12.180
"Can't kill you if you're already dead."

00:01:13.060 --> 00:01:17.060
The tonal whiplash has led some viewers to
craft theories about why Spider-Man's corner

00:01:17.069 --> 00:01:21.759
of the universe is so happy-go-lucky, just
months after everyone on Earth went through

00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:23.540
the most tragic events ever.

00:01:23.640 --> 00:01:27.560
This doesn't feel like a world that's been
through the apocalypse, so what if it isn't?

00:01:27.560 --> 00:01:32.759
What if the world of Far From Home never experienced
Thanos' Decimation, because the Avengers managed

00:01:32.760 --> 00:01:35.160
to go back in time and stop it from ever happening?

00:01:35.409 --> 00:01:39.120
We all know in our hearts that the heroes
who died from Thanos' snap will be coming

00:01:39.120 --> 00:01:43.900
back to life one way or another, if only because
the world demands a sequel to Black Panther.

00:01:44.069 --> 00:01:48.039
The default assumption is that the Avengers
will beat Thanos, revive the trillions of

00:01:48.039 --> 00:01:50.330
dead people, and then proceed from there.

00:01:50.330 --> 00:01:55.149
In that potential sequence of events, everyone
would still have knowledge of the Decimation

00:01:55.149 --> 00:01:56.149
happening.

00:01:56.149 --> 00:01:58.799
People would be back to life, but the pain
of loss would linger.

00:01:58.799 --> 00:02:02.889
So far at least, that does not seem to be
what's happening in Spider-Man: Far From Home.

00:02:02.889 --> 00:02:07.419
There’s another theory out there: Far From
Home might secretly be a prequel to Infinity

00:02:07.419 --> 00:02:12.560
War, taking place after Homecoming but before
Peter ditched his school bus and saved Iron

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:13.900
Man from getting beaten up.

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:18.030
But according to the filmmakers, this doesn't
seem to be the case.

00:02:18.030 --> 00:02:22.650
According to Amy Pascal, one of the producers
of Far From Home, the Spider-Man sequel will,

00:02:22.650 --> 00:02:26.260
quote, "start a few minutes after Avengers
4 wraps as a story."

00:02:26.560 --> 00:02:28.120
And it's not just her saying that.

00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:32.840
Marvel Studios head Kevin Feige has said the
same thing, promising audiences that Far From

00:02:32.849 --> 00:02:36.870
Home is indeed set after Infinity War and
Endgame.

00:02:36.870 --> 00:02:41.390
According to the MCU producer, Peter will
return to a, quote, "normal life" in Far From

00:02:41.390 --> 00:02:41.880
Home.

00:02:42.040 --> 00:02:45.220
Of course, it's always possible that the producers
are straight-up lying.

00:02:45.520 --> 00:02:47.340
"Alright then, keep your secrets."

00:02:47.340 --> 00:02:47.840
"Hnuhmm?"

00:02:48.060 --> 00:02:52.480
If it's true that Far From Home takes place
after the events of Endgame, then we're left

00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:53.880
with one big question.

00:02:54.069 --> 00:02:58.900
How will the story wrap up in a way that fits
with the lighthearted tone of Far From Home?

00:02:58.909 --> 00:03:03.349
Reversing the Decimation by bringing people
back to life in Endgame would presumably leave

00:03:03.349 --> 00:03:07.750
the people of Earth feeling pretty shaken
up at the start of the Spider-Man sequel.

00:03:07.750 --> 00:03:12.560
Even if Thanos' victims didn't remember being
dead, the loved ones they left behind certainly

00:03:12.560 --> 00:03:13.060
would.

00:03:13.100 --> 00:03:17.200
If that were the case, then forget about going
to Europe, Aunt May probably wouldn't let

00:03:17.200 --> 00:03:18.220
Peter leave the house.

00:03:18.480 --> 00:03:19.420
"And if you die, I feel like that's on me.

00:03:22.960 --> 00:03:24.359
I don't need that on my conscience."

00:03:24.360 --> 00:03:26.240
"Not a fan of that Tony Stark."

00:03:26.380 --> 00:03:30.670
All this adds up as evidence for the theory
that the Avengers will spend Endgame altering

00:03:30.670 --> 00:03:35.170
the timeline to ensure that Thanos never accomplishes
his genocidal goal.

00:03:35.170 --> 00:03:39.340
Some believe that the Far From Home trailer
all-but-confirms this theory, which is going

00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:43.360
back to basics in a way that seems impossible
in a world after the Snap.

00:03:43.520 --> 00:03:47.580
There's already a lot of evidence that Endgame's
plot will heavily involve time travel.

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:52.020
Looking over all the information that we have
at this point, a timeline reset seems more

00:03:52.020 --> 00:03:53.180
plausible than ever.

00:03:53.360 --> 00:03:55.020
Of course, all of this could change.

00:03:55.170 --> 00:03:59.220
Maybe we're being played by the marketing,
and Marvel has a huge surprise in store for

00:03:59.240 --> 00:04:00.800
us that no one will see coming..

